{"gene_id": "850504", "symbol": "ACT1", "description": "actin", "tax_id": "559292", "taxname": "Saccharomyces cerevisiae S288C", "type": "PROTEIN_CODING", "orientation": "minus", "chromosomes": ["VI"], "nomenclature_authority": {"authority": "SGD", "identifier": "S000001855"}, "synonyms": ["ABY1", "END7"], "annotations": [{"assembly_accession": "GCF_000146045.2", "assembly_name": "R64", "annotation_name": "SGD R64-5-1", "annotation_release_date": "2026-07-10", "genomic_locations": [{"genomic_accession_version": "NC_001138.5", "sequence_name": "VI", "genomic_range": {"begin": "53260", "end": "54696", "orientation": "minus"}}]}], "transcript_count": 1, "protein_count": 1, "transcript_type_counts": [{"type": "PROTEIN_CODING", "count": 1}], "gene_groups": [{"id": "850504", "method": "NCBI Ortholog"}], "summary": [{"description": "Enables ATP binding activity; ATP hydrolysis activity; and identical protein binding activity. A structural constituent of cytoskeleton. Involved in several processes, including ascospore wall assembly; mitotic actomyosin contractile ring contraction; and vacuole inheritance. Located in actin cytoskeleton; chromatin; and nucleus. Part of Ino80 complex; NuA4 histone acetyltransferase complex; and Swr1 complex. Used to study several diseases, including Baraitser-Winter syndrome 1; artery disease (multiple); autosomal dominant nonsyndromic deafness 20; intestinal atresia; and patent ductus arteriosus. Human ortholog(s) of this gene implicated in several diseases, including Baraitser-Winter syndrome 1; artery disease (multiple); congenital myopathy (multiple); intrinsic cardiomyopathy (multiple); and male infertility (multiple). Orthologous to several human genes including ACTA1 (actin alpha 1, skeletal muscle); ACTC1 (actin alpha cardiac muscle 1); and ACTB (actin beta). [provided by Alliance of Genome Resources, Jun 2026]"}], "gene_ontology": {"assigned_by": "SGD", "molecular_functions": [{"name": "ATP binding", "go_id": "GO:0005524", "evidence_c